      "message": "It\u0027s irrelevant to this CL. During code review, I saw the CL 430530 already removed GPIO_PULL_UP flag for USB_CX_5V_EN as they\u0027re output. Actually, it\u0027s correct. In datasheet section 4.5.2, it mentioned \"When the GPIO pin is configured as an output port, the internal pull-up or pull-down is disabled.\". \n\nI also saw gru and reef enable GPIO_PULL_UP as USB_CX_5V_EN are output. It\u0027s no harm if we only want to keep voltage. (They\u0027re push-pull and needn\u0027t pull-down/up resistance.) But if there\u0027s an application uses pin\u0027s internal weak resistance, it should be careful when pin is configured as output.",
